# Shopify Storefront credentials (PUBLIC — safe to ship in the frontend bundle).
# These are read at build time by Vite. After changing values, restart `vite dev`
# or trigger a fresh Netlify deploy. Set the same values in Netlify →
# Site settings → Environment variables.
#
# Where to find them:
#   - VITE_SHOPIFY_DOMAIN           → Shopify admin → Settings → Domains → your "myshopify.com" URL
#   - VITE_SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_TOKEN → Shopify admin → Apps → Headless / Buy Button → Storefront API access token
#   - VITE_SHOPIFY_COLLECTION_ID    → ID of the collection used to wire up the Buy Button SDK cart
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - DO NOT put any Admin API keys, secret keys, webhook secrets, or
#     password-protected tokens in this file. Storefront tokens are
#     intentionally read-only and rate-limited.
#   - This file is committed to git as a template. Copy it to `.env`
#     locally (which IS gitignored) and fill in real values there.
VITE_SHOPIFY_DOMAIN=your-shop.myshopify.com
VITE_SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_TOKEN=your-storefront-access-token
VITE_SHOPIFY_COLLECTION_ID=000000000000
